Root cause:
The bug was caused by the handling of unaligned memory accesses in user-land, which were incorrectly reported as SIGSEGV (segmentation fault) instead of SIGBUS (bus error) after the changes made in commit 52d7523. This misclassification led to improper signaling for unaligned access faults, which should have been reported as SIGBUS, consistent with the expected behavior prior to that commit. The patch corrects this by modifying the `do_bad_area` function to use a fault information table that correctly maps the exception status register (esr) values to the appropriate signals and codes for user-land faults.
